{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1ux:000001:issue_created:sase-1ux:8859db4dbaa980d7d70128877e62f5ce6f57e303a9f17629d4030059da7d8398","timestamp":"2026-11-22T13:33:06Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.1f4","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1ux","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1ux","title":"Make failed agent sessions and clans unmistakable","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-22T13:33:06Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.1f4","updated_at":"2026-11-22T13:33:06Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"When an agent session or clan stops on a failure, every Agents-tab surface says so: the row, the BY_STATUS section, the count chips, the waves and jump strips, and the detail panels all read FAILED and agree with each other. The cause and the next step are one glance away. A staged handoff the host refused to adopt shows as NOT ADOPTED, never as a phantom RUNNING with a ticking clock.","design":"plan:202611/failed_clan_visibility.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/failed_clan_visibility.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
